It modifies and builds AZ-MODS (https://github.com/Kyle-Hosman/xdj-az-mods, GPL-3.0-only,
Copyright (C) 2026 Kyle Hosman), whose source the launcher downloads at the commit named in
azmods/BASE. It is not part of AZ-MODS and not an official AZ-MODS release. It is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by AlphaTheta Corporation or Pioneer DJ. No part
of the deck's firmware is included here.

Third-party parts
-----------------

community/include/azmod-mod.h
  The AZ-MODS mod interface, the AZ-MODS SDK's header (https://github.com/Kyle-Hosman/az-mods-sdk),
  GPL-3.0-only, unchanged.

azmods/files/src/azmod/heb_glyphs.h and azmods/files/src/azmod/heb_keys.h
  Hebrew glyph outlines and key images made from DejaVu Sans Bold by
  azmods/files/tools/hebrew-assets.py. DejaVu fonts, Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc.
  (Bitstream Vera is a trademark of Bitstream, Inc.); DejaVu changes are in the public
  domain. Bitstream Vera Fonts license, full text in
  azmods/files/src/azmod/LICENSE-DEJAVU-FONTS, https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/License.html

azmods/files/src/azmod/bidi_tables.h
  Generated from the Unicode Character Database (BidiBrackets.txt, BidiMirroring.txt and
  the Bidi_Class property). Unicode data files: Copyright (c) Unicode, Inc., Unicode
  License v3, https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

What the launcher downloads to build (pinned by SHA-256 in launcher/build-azmod.sh, not
included here): Bootlin's aarch64 glibc toolchain (https://toolchains.bootlin.com) and
Ubuntu 18.04's arm64 libx11, libxext, libfreetype and x11proto packages, each under its
own license.
